pposed to the commonly-used variants
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-a=
scii-whitespace" id=3D"ref-for-split-on-ascii-whitespace">for ASCII whitesp=
ace</a> and
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-c=
ommas" id=3D"ref-for-split-on-commas">for commas</a> below, which are both =
more lenient in various ways involving
interspersed <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.or=
g/#ascii-whitespace" id=3D"ref-for-ascii-whitespace=E2=91=A4">ASCII whitesp=
ace</a>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" =
data-lt=3D"split on ASCII whitespace|split a string on ASCII whitespace" id=
=3D"split-on-ascii-whitespace">split a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=
=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A0">string</a> <var>input</var> on ASCII =
whitespace</dfn>:

</p>
   <ol>
    <li>
     <p>Let <var>position</var> be a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"http=
s://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-position-variable" id=3D"ref-for-string-p=
osition-variable=E2=91=A2">position variable</a> for <var>input</var>, init=
ially
 pointing at the start of <var>input</var>.

 </p>
    </li><li>
     <p>Let <var>tokens</var> be a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:=
//infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5">list</a> of <a =
data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D=
"ref-for-string=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A1">strings</a>, initially empty.

 </p>
    </li><li>
     <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#sk=
ip-ascii-whitespace" id=3D"ref-for-skip-ascii-whitespace">Skip ASCII whites=
pace</a> within <var>input</var> given <var>position</var>.

 </p>
    </li><li>
     <p>While <var>position</var> is not past the end of <var>input</var>:

  </p>
     <ol>
