   <h3 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"4.8" id=3D"time"><span class=
=3D"secno">4.8. </span><span class=3D"content">Time</span><a class=3D"self-=
link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#time"></a></h3>
   <p>Represent time using the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://w3=
c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-moment" id=3D"ref-for-dfn-moment">moment</a> and <=
a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-duratio=
n" id=3D"ref-for-dfn-duration">duration</a> specification types. Follow the=
 advice in
<a href=3D"https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#sec-tools"><cite>High Resolution =
Time</cite> =C2=A7=E2=80=AF3 Tools for Specification Authors</a> when creat=
ing these and exchanging them with JavaScript. <a data-link-type=3D"biblio"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-hr-time" title=3D"High Resol=
ution Time">[HR-TIME]</a>


</p>
   <h3 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"4.9" id=3D"singleton"><span =
class=3D"secno">4.9. </span><span class=3D"content">Singletons</span><a cla=
ss=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#singleton"></a></h3=
>
   <p>The following types can be used as inputs or outputs of algorithmic p=
rose to improve comprehension.
They have no observable representation beyond their effect on the flow of a=
ny given algorithm, and
they can only be compared with "is".</p>
   <dl>
    <dt><dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" i=
d=3D"allowed">allowed</dfn>
=20
    </dt><dd>
     <p>Indicates that some operation is permitted, often used in oppositio=
n to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#block=
ed" id=3D"ref-for-blocked">blocked</a>.

 </p>
    </dd><dt><dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=
=3D"" id=3D"blocked">blocked</dfn>
=20
    </dt><dd>
     <p>Indicates that some operation is not permitted, often used in oppos=
ition to
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#allowed" =
id=3D"ref-for-allowed">allowed</a>.

 </p>
    </dd><dt><dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=
=3D"" id=3D"failure">failure</dfn>
=20
    </dt><dd>
     <p>Indicates that some operation did not proceed as expected, often us=
ed in opposition to
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#success" =
id=3D"ref-for-success">success</a> or in combination with a more concrete t=
ype.

 </p>
    </dd><dt><dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=
=3D"" id=3D"success">success</dfn>
=20
    </dt><dd>
     <p>Indicates that some operation proceeded as expected, often used in =
opposition to
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#failure" =
id=3D"ref-for-failure">failure</a>.
</p>
   </dd></dl>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-singleton-return-and-comparison">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-s=
ingleton-return-and-comparison"></a>
=20
    <p>The following algorithm returns <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#success" id=3D"ref-for-success=E2=91=A0">succe=
ss</a> or <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
failure" id=3D"ref-for-failure=E2=91=A0">failure</a>:

 </p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>If something unexpectedly bad happened, then return <a data-link-t=
ype=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#failure" id=3D"ref-for-f=
ailure=E2=91=A1">failure</a>.
  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg=
.org/#success" id=3D"ref-for-success=E2=91=A1">success</a>.
 </p>
    </li></ol>
    <p>Callers of that algorithm might evaluate the result as follows:

 </p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>If <var>result</var> is <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://=
infra.spec.whatwg.org/#failure" id=3D"ref-for-failure=E2=91=A2">failure</a>=
, then shut everything down gracefully and abort.
  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A8">Assert</a>: <var>result</var> is <a d=
ata-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#success" id=3D=
"ref-for-success=E2=91=A2">success</a>.
  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>=E2=80=A6
 </p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-singleton-failure">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-s=
ingleton-failure"></a>
=20
    <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#fai=
lure" id=3D"ref-for-failure=E2=91=A3">Failure</a> is often used as the resu=
lt of an algorithm that can fail or return a value:

 </p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>If <var>status</var> is less than 200 or greater than 599, then re=
turn <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#failu=
re" id=3D"ref-for-failure=E2=91=A4">failure</a>.

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <var>status</var>.
 </p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <h2 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5" id=3D"data-structures"><s=
pan class=3D"secno">5. </span><span class=3D"content">Data structures</span=
><a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#data-structu=
res"></a></h2>
   <p>Conventionally, specifications have operated on a variety of vague sp=
ecification-level data
structures, based on shared understanding of their semantics. This generall=
y works well, but can
lead to ambiguities around edge cases, such as iteration order or what happ=
ens when you
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-append=
" id=3D"ref-for-set-append">append</a> an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=
">item</a> to an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatw=
g.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set">ordered set</a> that the set=
 already
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-conta=
in" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain">contains</a>. It has also led to a variety =
of divergent notation and phrasing, especially
around more complex data structures such as <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map">=
maps</a>.

</p>
   <p>This standard provides a small set of common data structures, along w=
ith notation and phrasing
for working with them, in order to create common ground.


</p>
   <h3 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.1" id=3D"lists"><span clas=
s=3D"secno">5.1. </span><span class=3D"content">Lists</span><a class=3D"sel=
f-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lists"></a></h3>
   <p>A <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" i=
d=3D"list">list</dfn> is a specification type consisting of a finite ordere=
d sequence of
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" data-dfn-t=
ype=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"item" id=3D"list-item">items</dfn>.

</p>
   <p>For notational convenience, a literal syntax can be used to express <=
a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D=
"ref-for-list=E2=91=A8">lists</a>, by surrounding
the list with U+00AB (=C2=AB) and U+00BB (=C2=BB), and separating its <a da=
ta-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=
=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A1">items</a> with U+002C (,).
An indexing syntax can be used by providing a zero-based index into a list =
inside square brackets.
The index cannot be out-of-bounds, except when used with <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id=3D"ref-for=
-list-contain=E2=91=A0">exists</a>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-notation"><a class=3D"self-link"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-list-notation"></a>Let <var=
>example</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.=
whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">list</a> =C2=AB "<c=
ode>a</code>",
"<code>b</code>", "<code>c</code>", "<code>a</code>" =C2=BB. Then <var>exam=
ple</var>[1] is the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wh=
atwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A6">string</a>
"<code>b</code>".

</p>
   <p>For notational convenience, a multiple assignment syntax may be used =
to assign multiple variables
to the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lis=
t" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A0">list</a>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-ty=
pe=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-=
list-item=E2=91=A2">items</a>, by surrounding the variables to be assigned =
with
U+00AB (=C2=AB) and U+00BB (=C2=BB) (same as lists), and separating each va=
riable name with U+002C (,). The
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A1">list</a>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D=
"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-=
size">size</a> must be the same as the number of variables to be assigned. =
Each
variable given is then set to the value of the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hr=
ef=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=
=91=A2">list</a>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.=
spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A3">item</a> at t=
he
corresponding index.

</p>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-multiple-assignment">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-l=
ist-multiple-assignment"></a>
=20
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>value</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"http=
s://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">list=
</a> =C2=AB "<code>a</code>", "<code>b</code>", "<code>c</code>" =C2=BB.

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Let =C2=AB <var>a</var>, <var>b</var>, <var>c</var> =C2=BB be <var=
>value</var>.

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">Assert</a>: <var>a</var> is =
"<code>a</code>".

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A0">Assert</a>: <var>b</var> is =
"<code>b</code>".

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A1">Assert</a>: <var>c</var> is =
"<code>c</code>".
 </p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <p>When a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.or=
g/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A4">list</a>=E2=80=99s contents =
are not fully controlled, as is the case for lists from user input,
the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" =
id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5">list</a>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-li=
st-size=E2=91=A0">size</a> should be checked to ensure it is the expected s=
ize before
list multiple assignment syntax is used.

</p>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-multiple-assignment-size">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-l=
ist-multiple-assignment-size"></a>
=20
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>If <var>list</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"htt=
ps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-size=E2=91=A1">si=
ze</a> is not <code>3</code>, then return failure.
  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Let =C2=AB <var>a</var>, <var>b</var>, <var>c</var> =C2=BB be <var=
>list</var>.
 </p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <hr>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-append">append</dfn> to a <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=
=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">list</a> that is not an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=
=E2=91=A0">ordered set</a> is to
add the given <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A4">item</a> to the end of the=
 list.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-extend">extend</dfn> a <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A0=E2=91=A7">list</a> that is not an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"=
https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=
=A1">ordered set</a> <var>A</var> with a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">list</a> <var>B</var>, <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-list-iterate=E2=91=A5">for each</a> <var>item</var> of <var>B</var>, <a d=
ata-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-append" i=
d=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A1">append</a> <var>item</var> to <=
var>A</var>.

</p>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-extend">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-l=
ist-extend"></a>
=20
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>ghostbusters</var> be =C2=AB "<code>Erin Gilbert</code>",=
 "<code>Abby Yates</code>" =C2=BB.

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#l=
ist-extend" id=3D"ref-for-list-extend">Extend</a> <var>ghostbusters</var> w=
ith =C2=AB "<code>Jillian Holtzmann</code>",
  "<code>Patty Tolan</code>" =C2=BB.

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2">Assert</a>: <var>ghostbuster=
s</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-size=E2=91=A2">size</a> is 4.

  </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">Assert</a>: <var>ghostbuster=
s</var>[2] is "<code>Jillian Holtzmann</code>".
 </p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-prepend">prepend</dfn> to a <a data-link-t=
ype=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=
=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">list</a> that is not an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=
=E2=91=A2">ordered set</a> is to
add the given <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A5">item</a> to the beginning =
of the list.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-replace">replace</dfn> within a <a data-li=
nk-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-=
list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">list</a> that is not an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" h=
ref=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-se=
t=E2=91=A3">ordered set</a> is
to replace all items from the list that match a given condition with the gi=
ven <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-i=
tem" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A6">item</a>,
or do nothing if none do.

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">The above definitions are modified when =
the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" =
id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A1">list</a> is an <a data-link-type=3D"d=
fn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-order=
ed-set=E2=91=A4">ordered set</a>; see
below for <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
set-append" id=3D"ref-for-set-append=E2=91=A0">ordered set append</a>, <a d=
ata-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-prepend" i=
d=3D"ref-for-set-prepend">prepend</a>, and
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-replac=
e" id=3D"ref-for-set-replace">replace</a>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,set" data-dfn-type=
=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-insert">insert</dfn> an <a data-link-t=
ype=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for=
-list-item=E2=91=A7">item</a> into a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"http=
s://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A2">list=
</a> before an
index is to add the given item to the list between the given index =E2=88=
=92 1 and the given index. If
the given index is 0, then <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.=
spec.whatwg.org/#list-prepend" id=3D"ref-for-list-prepend">prepend</a> the =
given item to the list.

</p>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"remove" data-algorithm-for=3D=
"list,set">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,set" data-dfn-typ=
e=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-remove">remove</dfn> zero or more <a =
data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=
=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A8">items</a> from a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" =
href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=
=91=A3">list</a>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>sizeBefore</var> be <var>list</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-lin=
k-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-=
for-list-size=E2=91=A3">size</a>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Remove all items from the list that match a given condition, or do=
 nothing if none do.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return true if <var>list</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-size=
=E2=91=A4">size</a> is less than <var>sizeBefore</var>; otherwise false.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-remove">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-l=
ist-remove"></a>
=20
    <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lis=
t-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove">Removing</a> <var>x</var> from the <a =
data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"r=
ef-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A4">list</a> =C2=AB <var>x</var>, <var>y</var>, =
<var>z</var>, <var>x</var> =C2=BB is to remove all
 items from the list that are equal to <var>x</var>. The list now is equiva=
lent to =C2=AB <var>y</var>, <var>z</var> =C2=BB.

 </p>
    <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lis=
t-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove=E2=91=A0">Removing</a> all items that s=
tart with the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A7">string</a> "<code>a</co=
de>" from the
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A5">list</a> =C2=AB "<code>a</code>", "<cod=
e>b</code>", "<code>ab</code>", "<code>ba</code>" =C2=BB is to
 remove the items "<code>a</code>" and "<code>ab</code>". The list is now e=
quivalent to =C2=AB
 "<code>b</code>", "<code>ba</code>" =C2=BB.
</p>
   </div>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" d=
ata-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-empty">empty</dfn> a <a da=
ta-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref=
-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A6">list</a> is to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove=
=E2=91=A1">remove</a>
all of its <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">items</a>.

</p>
   <p>A <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#li=
st" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A7">list</a> <dfn class=3D"dfn-panele=
d" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=
=3D"" data-lt=3D"contain|exist" id=3D"list-contain">contains</dfn> an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item"=
 id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A0">item</a> if it appears in the l=
ist. We can also denote this by saying that, for a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A8">list</a> <var>list</var> and an index <=
var>index</var>, "<var>list</var>[<var>index</var>] <a data-link-type=3D"df=
n" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id=3D"ref-for-list-=
contain=E2=91=A1">exists</a>".

</p>
   <p>A <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#li=
st" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=93=AA">list</a>=E2=80=99s <dfn class=3D"=
dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" da=
ta-export=3D"" id=3D"list-size">size</dfn> is the number of
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item"=
 id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A1">items</a> the list <a data-link=
-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id=3D"re=
f-for-list-contain=E2=91=A2">contains</a>.

</p>
   <p>A <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#li=
st" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A0">list</a> <dfn class=3D"dfn-panele=
d" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=
=3D"" data-lt=3D"is empty|is not empty" id=3D"list-is-empty">is empty</dfn>=
 if
its <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-s=
ize" id=3D"ref-for-list-size=E2=91=A5">size</a> is zero.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" d=
ata-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"get the indices|indices" i=
d=3D"list-get-the-indices">get the indices</dfn> of a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A1">list</a>, return <a data-link-type=3D"d=
fn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#the-exclusive-range" id=3D"ref-f=
or-the-exclusive-range=E2=91=A1">the range</a> from 0 to the list=E2=80=99s
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size"=
 id=3D"ref-for-list-size=E2=91=A6">size</a>, exclusive.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,set" data-dfn-type=
=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"iterate|for each" id=3D"list-iterate">=
iterate</dfn> over a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.w=
hatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A2">list</a>, performing=
 a
set of steps on each <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.w=
hatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2">item</a> i=
n order, use phrasing of the form
"<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iter=
ate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A6">For each</a> <var>item</var> of <=
var>list</var>", and then operate on <var>item</var> in the
subsequent prose.

</p>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"slice">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" =
data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-slice">slice</dfn> a <a d=
ata-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"re=
f-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A3">list</a> <var>list</var>, with an optional
integer <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list/slice" data-dfn-typ=
e=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-slice-from"><var>from</var></dfn> (de=
fault 0) and an optional integer
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list/slice" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn=
" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-slice-to"><var>to</var></dfn> (default <var>l=
ist</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wh=
atwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-size=E2=91=A7">size</a>), perform t=
he
following steps. They return a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://in=
fra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A4">list</a> o=
f the same designation as <var>list</var>.

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A4">Assert</a>: <var>from</var> =
is greater than or equal to 0.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5">Assert</a>: <var>to</var> is=
 less than or equal to <var>list</var>=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" =
href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-size=
=E2=91=A8">size</a>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">Assert</a>: <var>to</var> is=
 greater than or equal to <var>from</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Let <var>slice</var> be a new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A5">li=
st</a> of the same designation as <var>list</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#l=
ist-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A7">For each</a> <var>i</var>=
 of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#the-ex=
clusive-range" id=3D"ref-for-the-exclusive-range=E2=91=A2">the range</a> <v=
ar>from</var> to <var>to</var>,
 exclusive: <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org=
/#list-append" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2">append</a> <var=
>list</var>[<var>i</var>] to <var>slice</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <var>slice</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"has duplicates" data-algorith=
m-for=3D"list">
    <p>To check if a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.w=
hatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A6">list</a> <var>list</=
var> <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn"=
 data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-has-duplicates">has duplicates</dfn>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>seenItems</var> be =C2=AB =C2=BB.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#l=
ist-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A8">For each</a> <var>item</v=
ar> of <var>list</var>:

  </p>
      <ol>
       <li>
        <p>If <var>seenItems</var> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:=
//infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain=E2=91=A3"=
>contains</a> <var>item</var>, then return true.</p>
       </li><li>
        <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list-append" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">Append</a> <var>=
item</var> to <var>seenItems</var>.</p>
      </li></ol>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return false.</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" d=
ata-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-clone">clone</dfn> a <a da=
ta-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref=
-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A7">list</a> <var>list</var> is to return a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-slice=
" id=3D"ref-for-list-slice">slice</a> of <var>list</var>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">This is a "shallow clone", as the <a dat=
a-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D=
"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">items</a> themselves are not cloned i=
n
any way.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-clone"><a class=3D"self-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-list-clone"></a>Let <var>origi=
nal</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatw=
g.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A5">ordered set</a> =C2=
=AB
"<code>a</code>", "<code>b</code>", "<code>c</code>" =C2=BB. <a data-link-t=
ype=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-clone" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-list-clone">Cloning</a> <var>original</var> creates
a new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#orde=
red-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A6">ordered set</a> <var>clone</va=
r>, so that <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org=
/#set-replace" id=3D"ref-for-set-replace=E2=91=A0">replacing</a> "<code>a</=
code>" with
"<code>foo</code>" in <var>clone</var> gives =C2=AB "<code>foo</code>", "<c=
ode>b</code>", "<code>c</code>" =C2=BB,
while <var>original</var>[0] is still the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A5=E2=91=
=A8">string</a> "<code>a</code>".

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" d=
ata-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"list-reverse">reverse</dfn> a <=
a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D=
"ref-for-list=E2=91=A2=E2=91=A8">list</a> <var>list</var> is to create a ne=
w
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=93=AA">list</a> <var>reversed</var>, of the sa=
me designation, and, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.w=
hatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">for =
each</a> <var>item</var> of <var>list</var>,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-prepe=
nd" id=3D"ref-for-list-prepend=E2=91=A0">prepend</a> <var>item</var> to <va=
r>reversed</var>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" d=
ata-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"sort in ascending order|so=
rting in ascending order|sort|sorting" id=3D"list-sort-in-ascending-order">=
sort in ascending order</dfn>
a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A0">list</a> <var>list</var>, with a less t=
han algorithm <var>lessThanAlgo</var>, is to create a new <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A3=E2=91=A1">list</a>
<var>sorted</var>, containing the same <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=
=91=A4">items</a> as <var>list</var> but sorted so that according to
<var>lessThanAlgo</var>, each item is less than the one following it, if an=
y. For items that sort the same
(i.e., for which <var>lessThanAlgo</var> returns false for both comparisons=
), their relative order in
<var>sorted</var> must be the same as it was in <var>list</var>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"list,stack,queue,set" d=
ata-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"sort in descending order|s=
orting in descending order" id=3D"list-sort-in-descending-order">sort in de=
scending order</dfn>
a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A2">list</a> <var>list</var>, with a less t=
han algorithm <var>lessThanAlgo</var>, is to create a new <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A3=E2=91=A3">list</a>
<var>sorted</var>, containing the same <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=
=91=A5">items</a> as <var>list</var> but sorted so that according to
<var>lessThanAlgo</var>, each item is less than the one preceding it, if an=
y. For items that sort the same
(i.e., for which <var>lessThanAlgo</var> returns false for both comparisons=
), their relative order in
<var>sorted</var> must be the same as it was in <var>list</var>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-list-sort"><a class=3D"self-link" hre=
f=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-list-sort"></a>Let <var>origina=
l</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.=
org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A4">list</a> =C2=AB (200, "<co=
de>OK</code>"),
(404, "<code>Not Found</code>"), (null, "<code>OK</code>") =C2=BB. <a data-=
link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-sort-in-ascen=
ding-order" id=3D"ref-for-list-sort-in-ascending-order">Sorting</a> <var>or=
iginal</var> in
ascending order, with <var>a</var> being less than <var>b</var> if <var>a</=
var>=E2=80=99s second <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.=
whatwg.org/#struct-item" id=3D"ref-for-struct-item=E2=91=A2">item</a> is
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-=
less-than" id=3D"ref-for-code-unit-less-than=E2=91=A0">code unit less than<=
/a> <var>b</var>=E2=80=99s second <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:/=
/infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-item" id=3D"ref-for-struct-item=E2=91=A3">it=
em</a>, gives the result =C2=AB (404,
"<code>Not Found</code>"), (200, "<code>OK</code>"), (null, "<code>OK</code=
>") =C2=BB.</p>
   <hr>
   <p>The <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A5">list</a> type originates from t=
he JavaScript specification (where it is capitalized, as
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-list-=
and-record-specification-type" id=3D"ref-for-sec-list-and-record-specificat=
ion-type">List</a>); we repeat some elements of its definition here for eas=
e of reference,
and provide an expanded vocabulary for manipulating <a data-link-type=3D"df=
n" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=
=E2=91=A6">lists</a>. Whenever JavaScript expects a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-list-=
and-record-specification-type" id=3D"ref-for-sec-list-and-record-specificat=
ion-type=E2=91=A0">List</a>, a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://in=
fra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A7">list</a> a=
s defined here can be used; they are the same type.
<a data-link-type=3D"biblio" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-=
ecma-262" title=3D"ECMAScript Language Specification">[ECMA-262]</a>

</p>
   <h4 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.1.1" id=3D"stacks"><span c=
lass=3D"secno">5.1.1. </span><span class=3D"content">Stacks</span><a class=
=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#stacks"></a></h4>
   <p>Some <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A3=E2=91=A8">lists</a> are designated as <d=
fn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"=
stack" id=3D"stack">stacks</dfn>. A stack is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hr=
ef=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=
=93=AA">list</a>,
but conventionally, the following operations are used to operate on it, ins=
tead of using
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-appen=
d" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A4">append</a>, <a data-link-ty=
pe=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-prepend" id=3D"ref-f=
or-list-prepend=E2=91=A1">prepend</a>, or <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove=E2=
=91=A2">remove</a>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"stack" data-dfn-type=3D=
"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"stack-push">push</dfn> onto a <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#stack" id=3D"ref-for-stack=
">stack</a> is to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#list-append" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5">append</a=
> to it.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"stack" data-dfn-type=3D=
"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"stack-pop">pop</dfn> from a <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#stack" id=3D"ref-for-stack=
=E2=91=A0">stack</a>: if the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infr=
a.spec.whatwg.org/#stack" id=3D"ref-for-stack=E2=91=A1">stack</a>
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-is-em=
pty" id=3D"ref-for-list-is-empty=E2=91=A0">is not empty</a>, then <a data-l=
ink-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-remove" id=3D"=
ref-for-list-remove=E2=91=A3">remove</a> its last <a data-link-type=3D"dfn"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=
=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">item</a> and return
it; otherwise, return nothing.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"stack" data-dfn-type=3D=
"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"stack-peek">peek</dfn> into a <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#stack" id=3D"ref-for-stack=
=E2=91=A2">stack</a>: if the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infr=
a.spec.whatwg.org/#stack" id=3D"ref-for-stack=E2=91=A3">stack</a>
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-is-em=
pty" id=3D"ref-for-list-is-empty=E2=91=A1">is not empty</a>, then return it=
s last <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lis=
t-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7">item</a>; otherwise, ret=
urn
nothing.

</p>
   <p>Although <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.=
org/#stack" id=3D"ref-for-stack=E2=91=A4">stacks</a> are <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A4=E2=91=A0">lists</a>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra=
.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=
=A0">for each</a> must not be used with them;
instead, a combination of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.s=
pec.whatwg.org/#iteration-while" id=3D"ref-for-iteration-while=E2=91=A2">wh=
ile</a> and <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org=
/#stack-pop" id=3D"ref-for-stack-pop">pop</a> is more appropriate.

</p>
   <h4 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.1.2" id=3D"queues"><span c=
lass=3D"secno">5.1.2. </span><span class=3D"content">Queues</span><a class=
=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#queues"></a></h4>
   <p>Some <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=91=A1">lists</a> are designated as <d=
fn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"=
queue" id=3D"queue">queues</dfn>. A queue is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hr=
ef=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=
=91=A2">list</a>,
but conventionally, the following operations are used to operate on it, ins=
tead of using
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-appen=
d" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">append</a>, <a data-link-ty=
pe=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-prepend" id=3D"ref-f=
or-list-prepend=E2=91=A2">prepend</a>, or <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove=E2=
=91=A4">remove</a>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"queue" data-dfn-type=3D=
"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"queue-enqueue">enqueue</dfn> in a <a data-link=
-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#queue" id=3D"ref-for-q=
ueue">queue</a> is to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.=
whatwg.org/#list-append" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7">appen=
d</a> to it.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"queue" data-dfn-type=3D=
"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"queue-dequeue">dequeue</dfn> from a <a data-li=
nk-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#queue" id=3D"ref-for=
-queue=E2=91=A0">queue</a> is to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://=
infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove=E2=91=A5">rem=
ove</a> its first
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item"=
 id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">item</a> and return it, if the =
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#queue" id=
=3D"ref-for-queue=E2=91=A1">queue</a> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"htt=
ps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-is-empty" id=3D"ref-for-list-is-empty=E2=
=91=A2">is not empty</a>, or to return
nothing if it is.

</p>
   <p>Although <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.=
org/#queue" id=3D"ref-for-queue=E2=91=A2">queues</a> are <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A4=E2=91=A3">lists</a>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra=
.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=
=A1">for each</a> must not be used with them;
instead, a combination of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.s=
pec.whatwg.org/#iteration-while" id=3D"ref-for-iteration-while=E2=91=A3">wh=
ile</a> and <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org=
/#queue-dequeue" id=3D"ref-for-queue-dequeue">dequeue</a> is more appropria=
te.

</p>
   <h4 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.1.3" id=3D"sets"><span cla=
ss=3D"secno">5.1.3. </span><span class=3D"content">Sets</span><a class=3D"s=
elf-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#sets"></a></h4>
   <p>Some <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=91=A4">lists</a> are designated as <d=
fn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"=
ordered set|set" id=3D"ordered-set">ordered sets</dfn>. An
ordered set is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatw=
g.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=91=A5">list</a> with the additi=
onal semantic that it must not contain the same
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item"=
 id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">item</a> twice.

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">Almost all cases on the web platform req=
uire an <em>ordered</em> set, instead of an
unordered one, since interoperability requires that any developer-exposed e=
numeration of the set=E2=80=99s
contents be consistent between browsers. In those cases where order is not =
important, we still use
ordered sets; implementations can optimize based on the fact that the order=
 is not observable.

</p>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"create" data-algorithm-for=3D=
"set">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-create">create</dfn> a <a data-link-type=3D=
"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ord=
ered-set=E2=91=A7">set</a>, given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https=
://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=91=A6">list<=
/a> <var>input</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>result</var> be an empty <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=
=E2=91=A8">set</a>.
 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#l=
ist-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2">For each</a> <va=
r>item</var> of <var>input</var>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:/=
/infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-append" id=3D"ref-for-set-append=E2=91=A1">appe=
nd</a> <var>item</var> to <var>result</var>.
 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <var>result</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-append">append</dfn> to an <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-=
ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">ordered set</a>: if the set <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-list-contain=E2=91=A4">contains</a>
the given <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">item</a>, then do not=
hing; otherwise, perform the normal <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https=
://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A4=E2=91=A7">list<=
/a>
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-appen=
d" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">append</a> operation.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-extend">extend</dfn> an <a data-link-type=3D=
"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ord=
ered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A0">ordered set</a> <var>A</var> with a <a data-lin=
k-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-l=
ist=E2=91=A4=E2=91=A8">list</a> <var>B</var>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hre=
f=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterat=
e=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">for each</a>
<var>item</var> of <var>B</var>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://=
infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-append" id=3D"ref-for-set-append=E2=91=A2">appen=
d</a> <var>item</var> to <var>A</var>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-prepend">prepend</dfn> to an <a data-link-ty=
pe=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A1">ordered set</a>: if the set
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-conta=
in" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain=E2=91=A5">contains</a> the given <a data-lin=
k-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-=
for-list-item=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A1">item</a>, then do nothing; otherwise, perf=
orm the
normal <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#lis=
t" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5=E2=93=AA">list</a> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-prepend" id=3D"ref-for-list-pr=
epend=E2=91=A3">prepend</a> operation.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"replace|replacing" id=3D"set-replace">repla=
ce</dfn> within an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wha=
twg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2">ordered =
set</a>
<var>set</var>, given <var>item</var> and <var>replacement</var>: if <var>s=
et</var>
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-conta=
in" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain=E2=91=A6">contains</a> <var>item</var> or <v=
ar>replacement</var>, then replace the first instance
of either with <var>replacement</var> and <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-remove" id=3D"ref-for-list-remove=E2=
=91=A6">remove</a> all other instances.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-set-replace"><a class=3D"self-link" h=
ref=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-set-replace"></a><a data-link=
-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-replace" id=3D"ref=
-for-set-replace=E2=91=A1">Replacing</a> "a" with "c" within the
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-se=
t" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">ordered set</a> =C2=AB "a",=
 "b", "c" =C2=BB gives =C2=AB "c", "b" =C2=BB. Within =C2=AB "c", "b", "a" =
=C2=BB it gives
=C2=AB "c", "b" =C2=BB as well.

</p>
   <p>An <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#o=
rdered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A4">ordered set</a> <v=
ar>set</var> is a <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-=
type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-subset">subset</dfn> of another <a =
data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" =
id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5">ordered set</a>
<var>superset</var> (and conversely, <var>superset</var> is a <dfn class=3D=
"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" i=
d=3D"set-superset">superset</dfn> of <var>set</var>) if,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-itera=
te" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A4">for each</a> <var>item</v=
ar> of <var>set</var>, <var>superset</var> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain=
=E2=91=A7">contains</a> <var>item</var>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">This implies that an <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-=
ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">ordered set</a> is both a <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-subset" id=3D"ref-for-s=
et-subset">subset</a> and a
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-supers=
et" id=3D"ref-for-set-superset">superset</a> of itself.

</p>
   <p>A <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#or=
dered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7">set</a> <var>A</var=
> is <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" =
data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-equal">equal</dfn> to a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn=
" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered=
-set=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">set</a> <var>B</var>
if <var>A</var> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.w=
hatwg.org/#set-subset" id=3D"ref-for-set-subset=E2=91=A0">subset</a> of <va=
r>B</var> and <var>A</var> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://i=
nfra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-superset" id=3D"ref-for-set-superset=E2=91=A0">su=
perset</a> of <var>B</var>.

</p>
   <p>The <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-intersection">intersection</dfn> of <a data=
-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=
=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">ordered sets</a> <var>A</var> an=
d <var>B</var>, is the result
of creating a new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">ordered s=
et</a> <var>set</var> and, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.=
spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5=
">for each</a> <var>item</var> of <var>A</var>, if <var>B</var>
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-conta=
in" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain=E2=91=A8">contains</a> <var>item</var>, <a d=
ata-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-append" id=
=3D"ref-for-set-append=E2=91=A3">appending</a> <var>item</var> to <var>set<=
/var>.

</p>
   <p>The <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-union">union</dfn> of <a data-link-type=3D"=
dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-orde=
red-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A1">ordered sets</a> <var>A</var> and <var>B</var>, =
is the result of
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-clone=
" id=3D"ref-for-list-clone=E2=91=A0">cloning</a> <var>A</var> as <var>set</=
var> and, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">for each</a> <v=
ar>item</var> of <var>B</var>,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-append=
" id=3D"ref-for-set-append=E2=91=A4">appending</a> <var>item</var> to <var>=
set</var>.

</p>
   <p>The <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"set" data-dfn-type=3D"=
dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"set-difference">difference</dfn> of <a data-lin=
k-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"re=
f-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A2">ordered sets</a> <var>A</var> and <var=
>B</var>, is the result
of creating a new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A3">ordered s=
et</a> <var>set</var> and, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.=
spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7=
">for each</a> <var>item</var> of <var>A</var>, if <var>B</var>
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-conta=
in" id=3D"ref-for-list-contain=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">does not contain</a> <var=
>item</var>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.or=
g/#set-append" id=3D"ref-for-set-append=E2=91=A5">appending</a> <var>item</=
var> to <var>set</var>.

</p>
   <hr>
   <p><dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" dat=
a-lt=3D"the range|the inclusive range" id=3D"the-range">The range</dfn> <va=
r>n</var> to <var>m</var>,
inclusive, creates a new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.sp=
ec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A4">or=
dered set</a> containing all of the integers from <var>n</var> up to
and including <var>m</var> in consecutively increasing order, as long as <v=
ar>m</var> is greater
than or equal to <var>n</var>.

</p>
   <p><dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" dat=
a-lt=3D"the exclusive range" id=3D"the-exclusive-range">The range</dfn> <va=
r>n</var> to <var>m</var>, exclusive,
creates a new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A5">ordered set</=
a> containing all of the integers from <var>n</var> up to and including
<var>m</var> =E2=88=92 1 in consecutively increasing order, as long as <var=
>m</var> is greater than
<var>n</var>. If <var>m</var> equals <var>n</var>, then it creates an empty=
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-s=
et" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A6">ordered set</a>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-the-range"><a class=3D"self-link" hre=
f=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-the-range"></a><a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-list-iterate=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">For each</a> <var>n</var> of <a data-link=
-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#the-range" id=3D"ref-f=
or-the-range">the range</a> 1 to
4, inclusive, =E2=80=A6


</p>
   <h3 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.2" id=3D"maps"><span class=
=3D"secno">5.2. </span><span class=3D"content">Maps</span><a class=3D"self-=
link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#maps"></a></h3>
   <p>An <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" =
data-lt=3D"ordered map|map" id=3D"ordered-map">ordered map</dfn>, or someti=
mes just "map", is a
specification type consisting of a finite ordered sequence of <a data-link-=
type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-tu=
ple=E2=91=A2">tuples</a>, each consisting
of a <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" =
data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-key">key</dfn> and a <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" =
data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-value=
">value</dfn>, with no key appearing
twice. Each such tuple is called an <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=
=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-entry">entry</dfn=
>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">As with <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=
=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A7">ordered sets</a>, by default we assume that maps need t=
o be ordered for
interoperability among implementations.

</p>
   <p>A literal syntax can be used to express <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hre=
f=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=
=E2=91=A0">ordered maps</a>, by starting an ordered map with
U+00AB (=C2=AB) and U+005B ([), ending it with U+005D (]) and U+00BB (=C2=
=BB), separating each
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry"=
 id=3D"ref-for-map-entry">entry</a>=E2=80=99s <var>key</var> and <var>value=
</var> with U+2192 (=E2=86=92), and separating its entries with
U+002C (,).

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-map-notation"><a class=3D"self-link" =
href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-map-notation"></a>Let <var>e=
xample</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wh=
atwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1">ordered map</a> =
=C2=AB[
"<code>a</code>" =E2=86=92 `<code>x</code>`, "<code>b</code>" =E2=86=92 `<c=
ode>y</code>` ]=C2=BB. Then
<var>example</var>["<code>a</code>"] is the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#byte-sequence" id=3D"ref-for-byte-sequen=
ce=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7">byte sequence</a> `<code>x</code>`.

</p>
   <hr>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"get|get the value" id=3D"map-get">get the v=
alue of an entry</dfn> in an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-ma=
p" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A2">ordered map</a> <var>map</var> given=
 a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-key=
" id=3D"ref-for-map-key">key</a> <var>key</var> and an optional
<var>default</var>:

</p>
   <ol>
    <li>
     <p>If <var>map</var> does not <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:=
//infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-exists" id=3D"ref-for-map-exists">contain</a> =
<var>key</var> and <var>default</var>
 is given, then return <var>default</var>.

 </p>
    </li><li>
     <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#as=
sert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7">Assert</a>: <var>map</var> <a=
 data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-exists" =
id=3D"ref-for-map-exists=E2=91=A0">contains</a> <var>key</var>.

 </p>
    </li><li>
     <p>Return the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wha=
twg.org/#map-value" id=3D"ref-for-map-value">value</a> of the <a data-link-=
type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-map-entry=E2=91=A0">entry</a> in <var>map</var> whose
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-key" =
id=3D"ref-for-map-key=E2=91=A0">key</a> is <var>key</var>.
</p>
   </li></ol>
   <p>We can also denote <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.sp=
ec.whatwg.org/#map-get" id=3D"ref-for-map-get">getting the value of an entr=
y</a> using an indexing syntax,
by providing a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.=
org/#map-key" id=3D"ref-for-map-key=E2=91=A1">key</a> inside square bracket=
s directly following a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec=
.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A3">map</a>.
A default can be given by adding the phrase <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data=
-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-with-defa=
ult">with default</dfn> followed by the
default value.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-map-get"><a class=3D"self-link" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-map-get"></a>If <var>map</var>["=
<code>test</code>"]
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-exists=
" id=3D"ref-for-map-exists=E2=91=A1">exists</a>, then return <var>map</var>=
["<code>test</code>"].

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-map-get-with-default"><a class=3D"sel=
f-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-map-get-with-default=
"></a>Let <var>example</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https=
://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A4">=
ordered map</a>
=C2=AB[ "<code>a</code>" =E2=86=92 "<code>x</code>", "<code>b</code>" =E2=
=86=92 "<code>y</code>" ]=C2=BB. Then
<var>example</var>["<code>a</code>"] is the same as <var>example</var>["<co=
de>a</code>"] <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#map-with-default" id=3D"ref-for-map-with-default">with default</a> "<co=
de>z</code>",
namely "<code>x</code>". <var>example</var>["<code>c</code>"] would hit an =
assert.
<var>example</var>["<code>c</code>"] <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"http=
s://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-with-default" id=3D"ref-for-map-with-default=
=E2=91=A0">with default</a> "<code>z</code>" is "<code>z</code>".

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"set|set the value" id=3D"map-set">set the v=
alue of an entry</dfn> in an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-ma=
p" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A5">ordered map</a> to a given <a data-l=
ink-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-value" id=3D"re=
f-for-map-value=E2=91=A0">value</a> is to update the value of any existing
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry"=
 id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A1">entry</a> if the map <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-exists" id=3D"ref-for-m=
ap-exists=E2=91=A2">contains</a> an entry with the given <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-key" id=3D"ref-for-map-=
key=E2=91=A2">key</a>,
or if none such exists, to add a new entry with the given key/value to the =
end of the map. We can
also denote this by saying, for an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:=
//infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A6">o=
rdered map</a> <var>map</var>, key <var>key</var>, and value <var>value</va=
r>,
"<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-set" =
id=3D"ref-for-map-set">set</a> <var>map</var>[<var>key</var>] to <var>value=
</var>".

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"remove" id=3D"map-remove">remove an entry</=
dfn> from an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.or=
g/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A7">ordered map</a> is to r=
emove
all <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-en=
try" id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A2">entries</a> from the map that match =
a given condition, or do nothing if none do. If
the condition is having a certain <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:/=
/infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-key" id=3D"ref-for-map-key=E2=91=A3">key</a>, t=
hen we can also denote this by saying, for
an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered=
-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A8">ordered map</a> <var>map</var> an=
d key <var>key</var>, "<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec=
.whatwg.org/#map-remove" id=3D"ref-for-map-remove">remove</a> <var>map</var=
>[<var>key</var>]".

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-clear">clear</dfn> an <a data-link-type=3D"d=
fn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-order=
ed-map=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">ordered map</a> is to remove all <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry" id=3D"ref-for-m=
ap-entry=E2=91=A3">entries</a>
from the map.

</p>
   <p>An <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#o=
rdered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A0">ordered map</a> <d=
fn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-ex=
port=3D"" data-lt=3D"exist|contain" id=3D"map-exists">contains an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry"=
 id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A4">entry</a> with a given key</dfn> if ther=
e exists an entry with that <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra=
.spec.whatwg.org/#map-key" id=3D"ref-for-map-key=E2=91=A4">key</a>.
We can also denote this by saying that, for an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hr=
ef=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=
=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A1">ordered map</a> <var>map</var> and key <var>key</var>, =
"<var>map</var>[<var>key</var>]
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-exists=
" id=3D"ref-for-map-exists=E2=91=A3">exists</a>".

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"getting the keys|get the keys|keys" id=3D"m=
ap-getting-the-keys">get the keys</dfn> of an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-ma=
p" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A2">ordered map</a>, return a n=
ew <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered=
-set" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-set=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A8">ordered set</a> whose <a=
 data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" i=
d=3D"ref-for-list-item=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A2">items</a> are each of the
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-gettin=
g-the-keys" id=3D"ref-for-map-getting-the-keys">keys</a> in the map=E2=80=
=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-e=
ntry" id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A5">entries</a>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"getting the values|get the values|values" i=
d=3D"map-getting-the-values">get the values</dfn> of an
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-ma=
p" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A3">ordered map</a>, return a n=
ew <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" i=
d=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A0">list</a> whose <a data-link-type=3D"df=
n" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item" id=3D"ref-for-list-ite=
m=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A3">items</a> are each of the
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-gettin=
g-the-values" id=3D"ref-for-map-getting-the-values">values</a> in the map=
=E2=80=99s <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#map-entry" id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A6">entries</a>.

</p>
   <p>An <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#o=
rdered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A4">ordered map</a>=E2=
=80=99s <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"df=
n" data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-size">size</dfn> is the <a data-link-type=3D"=
dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id=3D"ref-for-list-s=
ize=E2=91=A0=E2=93=AA">size</a> of the result
of running <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#map-getting-the-keys" id=3D"ref-for-map-getting-the-keys=E2=91=A0">get the=
 keys</a> on the map.

</p>
   <p>An <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#o=
rdered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A5">ordered map</a> <d=
fn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-ex=
port=3D"" data-lt=3D"is empty|is not empty" id=3D"map-is-empty">is empty</d=
fn> if its
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-size" =
id=3D"ref-for-map-size">size</a> is zero.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"iterate|for each" id=3D"map-iterate">iterat=
e</dfn> over an <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg=
.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A6">ordered map=
</a>, performing
a set of steps on each <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec=
.whatwg.org/#map-entry" id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A7">entry</a> in orde=
r, use phrasing of the form
"<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-itera=
te" id=3D"ref-for-map-iterate=E2=91=A0">For each</a> <var>key</var> =E2=86=
=92 <var>value</var> of <var>map</var>", and then operate on <var>key</var>=
 and <var>value</var> in the
subsequent prose.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"map-clone">clone</dfn> an <a data-link-type=3D"d=
fn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-order=
ed-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A7">ordered map</a> <var>map</var> is to create a new
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-ma=
p" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">ordered map</a> <var>clone<=
/var>, and, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org=
/#map-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-map-iterate=E2=91=A1">for each</a> <var>key</v=
ar> =E2=86=92 <var>value</var> of <var>map</var>,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-set" i=
d=3D"ref-for-map-set=E2=91=A0">set</a> <var>clone</var>[<var>key</var>] to =
<var>value</var>.

</p>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">This is a "shallow clone", as the <a dat=
a-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-getting-the-=
keys" id=3D"ref-for-map-getting-the-keys=E2=91=A1">keys</a> and <a data-lin=
k-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-getting-the-value=
s" id=3D"ref-for-map-getting-the-values=E2=91=A0">values</a>
themselves are not cloned in any way.

</p>
   <p class=3D"example" id=3D"example-map-clone"><a class=3D"self-link" hre=
f=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-map-clone"></a>Let <var>origina=
l</var> be the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.=
org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">ordered map<=
/a> =C2=AB[
"<code>a</code>" =E2=86=92 =C2=AB1, 2, 3=C2=BB, "<code>b</code>" =E2=86=92 =
=C2=AB=C2=BB ]=C2=BB. <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.=
whatwg.org/#list-clone" id=3D"ref-for-list-clone=E2=91=A1">Cloning</a> <var=
>original</var> creates a
new <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordere=
d-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">ordered map</a> <var>cl=
one</var>, so that <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wha=
twg.org/#map-set" id=3D"ref-for-map-set=E2=91=A1">setting</a> <var>clone</v=
ar>["<code>a</code>"] to
=C2=AB-1, -2, -3=C2=BB gives =C2=AB[ "<code>a</code>" =E2=86=92 =C2=AB-1, -=
2, -3=C2=BB, "<code>b</code>" =E2=86=92 =C2=AB=C2=BB ]=C2=BB and leaves
<var>original</var> unchanged. However, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"h=
ttps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-append" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=
=A1=E2=93=AA">appending</a> 4 to <var>clone</var>["<code>b</code>"] will mo=
dify
the corresponding <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#map-value" id=3D"ref-for-map-value=E2=91=A1">value</a> in both <var=
>clone</var> and <var>original</var>, as they both point to the
same <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list"=
 id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A1">list</a>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"sort in ascending order|sorting in ascendin=
g order|sort|sorting" id=3D"map-sort-in-ascending-order">sort in ascending =
order</dfn>
a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-=
map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A1">map</a> <var>map</var>, w=
ith a less than algorithm <var>lessThanAlgo</var>, is to create a new <a da=
ta-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=
=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A2">map</a>
<var>sorted</var>, containing the same <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry" id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A8">e=
ntries</a> as <var>map</var> but sorted so that according to
<var>lessThanAlgo</var>, each entry is less than the one following it, if a=
ny. For entries that sort the same
(i.e., for which <var>lessThanAlgo</var> returns false for both comparisons=
), their relative order in
<var>sorted</var> must be the same as it was in <var>map</var>.

</p>
   <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"map" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"sort in descending order|sorting in descend=
ing order" id=3D"map-sort-in-descending-order">sort in descending order</df=
n>
a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-=
map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A3">map</a> <var>map</var>, w=
ith a less than algorithm <var>lessThanAlgo</var>, is to create a new <a da=
ta-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=
=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A4">map</a>
<var>sorted</var>, containing the same <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"ht=
tps://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#map-entry" id=3D"ref-for-map-entry=E2=91=A0=E2=
=93=AA">entries</a> as <var>map</var> but sorted so that according to
<var>lessThanAlgo</var>, each entry is less than the one preceding it, if a=
ny. For entries that sort the same
(i.e., for which <var>lessThanAlgo</var> returns false for both comparisons=
), their relative order in
<var>sorted</var> must be the same as it was in <var>map</var>.


</p>
   <h3 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.3" id=3D"structs"><span cl=
ass=3D"secno">5.3. </span><span class=3D"content">Structs</span><a class=3D=
"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#structs"></a></h3>
   <p>A <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" i=
d=3D"struct">struct</dfn> is a specification type consisting of a finite se=
t of
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"struct,tuple" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=3D"item" id=3D"struct-item">items</dfn>, each =
of which has a unique and immutable
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-for=3D"struct,tuple" data-dfn-type=3D"d=
fn" data-export=3D"" id=3D"struct-name">name</dfn>. An <a data-link-type=3D=
"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-item" id=3D"ref-for-str=
uct-item=E2=91=A4">item</a> holds a value of a defined type.

</p>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-struct">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-s=
truct"></a>
=20
    <p>An <dfn data-var-ignore=3D"">email</dfn> is an example <a data-link-=
type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" id=3D"ref-for-s=
truct=E2=91=A0">struct</a> consisting of a
 <dfn data-var-ignore=3D"">local part</dfn> (a string) and a <dfn data-var-=
ignore=3D"">host</dfn> (a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://url.spe=
c.whatwg.org/#concept-host" id=3D"ref-for-concept-host">host</a>).

 </p>
    <p>A nonsense algorithm might use this definition as follows:

 </p>
    <ol>
     <li>Let <var>email</var> be an email whose local part is "<code>hostma=
ster</code>" and host
  is <code>infra.example</code>.
 =20
     </li><li>=E2=80=A6
=20
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <h4 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"5.3.1" id=3D"tuples"><span c=
lass=3D"secno">5.3.1. </span><span class=3D"content">Tuples</span><a class=
=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuples"></a></h4>
   <p>A <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" i=
d=3D"tuple">tuple</dfn> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infr=
a.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" id=3D"ref-for-struct=E2=91=A1">struct</a> whose =
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-ite=
m" id=3D"ref-for-struct-item=E2=91=A5">items</a> are ordered. For
notational convenience, a literal syntax can be used to express <a data-lin=
k-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-=
tuple=E2=91=A3">tuples</a>, by surrounding the
tuple with parentheses and separating its <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D=
"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-item" id=3D"ref-for-struct-item=E2=
=91=A6">items</a> with U+002C (,). To use this
notation, the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.o=
rg/#struct-name" id=3D"ref-for-struct-name=E2=91=A0">names</a> need to be c=
lear from context. This can be done by preceding
the first instance with the name given to the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hre=
f=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-tuple=E2=91=A4">tu=
ple</a>. An indexing syntax can be used by
providing a zero-based index into a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https=
://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-tuple=E2=91=A5">tuple</a> in=
side square brackets. The index cannot be
out-of-bounds.

</p>
   <div class=3D"example" id=3D"example-tuple">
    <a class=3D"self-link" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#example-t=
uple"></a>
=20
    <p>A <dfn data-var-ignore=3D"">status</dfn> is an example <a data-link-=
type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-tu=
ple=E2=91=A6">tuple</a> consisting of a <dfn data-var-ignore=3D"">code</dfn=
> (a
 number) and <dfn data-var-ignore=3D"">text</dfn> (a byte sequence).

 </p>
    <p>A nonsense algorithm that manipulates status tuples for the purpose =
of demonstrating their
 usage is:</p>
    <ol>
     <li>Let <var>statusInstance</var> be the status (200, `<code>OK</code>=
`).
 =20
     </li><li>Set <var>statusInstance</var> to (301, `<code>FOO BAR</code>`=
).
 =20
     </li><li>If <var>statusInstance</var>=E2=80=99s code is 404, then =E2=
=80=A6
=20
    </li></ol>
    <p>The last step could also be written as "If <var>statusInstance</var>=
[0] is 404, then =E2=80=A6". This
 might be preferable if the <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra=
.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-tuple=E2=91=A7">tuple</a> <a data-li=
nk-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-name" id=3D"r=
ef-for-struct-name=E2=91=A1">names</a> do not have explicit definitions.
</p>
   </div>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">It is intentional that not all <a data-l=
ink-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" id=3D"ref-f=
or-struct=E2=91=A2">structs</a> are <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https=
://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=3D"ref-for-tuple=E2=91=A8">tuples</a>. =
Documents using the
Infra Standard might need the flexibility to add new <a data-link-type=3D"d=
fn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-name" id=3D"ref-for-struc=
t-name=E2=91=A2">names</a> to their struct
without breaking literal syntax used by their dependencies. In that case a =
tuple is not appropriate.


</p>
   <h2 class=3D"heading settled" data-level=3D"6" id=3D"json"><span class=
=3D"secno">6. </span><span class=3D"content">JSON</span><a class=3D"self-li=
nk" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#json"></a></h2>
   <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">The conventions used in the algorithms i=
n this section are those of the JavaScript
specification. <a data-link-type=3D"biblio" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#biblio-ecma-262" title=3D"ECMAScript Language Specification">[ECMA-=
262]</a>

</p>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"parse a JSON string to a Java=
Script value">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D""=
 id=3D"parse-a-json-string-to-a-javascript-value">parse a JSON string to a =
JavaScript value</dfn>, given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://i=
nfra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=93=AA">strin=
g</a> <var>string</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Return ? <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc39.gi=
thub.io/ecma262/#sec-call" id=3D"ref-for-sec-call">Call</a>(<a data-link-ty=
pe=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-json.parse" id=3D"re=
f-for-sec-json.parse">%JSON.parse%</a>, undefined, =C2=AB <var>string</var>=
 =C2=BB).
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"parse JSON bytes to a JavaScr=
ipt value">
    <p>To
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=
=3D"parse JSON bytes to a JavaScript value|parse JSON from bytes" id=3D"par=
se-json-bytes-to-a-javascript-value">parse JSON bytes to a JavaScript value=
</dfn>,
given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#by=
te-sequence" id=3D"ref-for-byte-sequence=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">byte sequence</=
a> <var>bytes</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>string</var> be the result of running <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-decode" id=3D"ref-=
for-utf-8-decode=E2=91=A2">UTF-8 decode</a> on <var>bytes</var>. <a data-li=
nk-type=3D"biblio" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-encoding" =
title=3D"Encoding Standard">[ENCODING]</a>

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return the result of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://inf=
ra.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-a-json-string-to-a-javascript-value" id=3D"ref-fo=
r-parse-a-json-string-to-a-javascript-value">parsing a JSON string to a Jav=
aScript value</a> given <var>string</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"serialize a JavaScript value =
to a JSON string">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D""=
 id=3D"serialize-a-javascript-value-to-a-json-string">serialize a JavaScrip=
t value to a JSON string</dfn>, given a JavaScript value
<var>value</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>result</var> be ? <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=
=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-call" id=3D"ref-for-sec-call=E2=91=
=A0">Call</a>(<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma=
262/#sec-json.stringify" id=3D"ref-for-sec-json.stringify">%JSON.stringify%=
</a>, undefined, =C2=AB <var>value</var> =C2=BB).

  </p>
      <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">Since no additional arguments are pas=
sed to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#se=
c-json.stringify" id=3D"ref-for-sec-json.stringify=E2=91=A0">%JSON.stringif=
y%</a>, the resulting
  string will have no whitespace inserted.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>If <var>result</var> is undefined, then throw a <code class=3D"idl=
"><a data-link-type=3D"idl" href=3D"https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#excepti=
ondef-typeerror" id=3D"ref-for-exceptiondef-typeerror=E2=91=A0">TypeError</=
a></code>.

  </p>
      <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">This can happen if <var>value</var> d=
oes not have a JSON representation, e.g., if
  it is undefined or a function.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A0=E2=91=A8">Assert</a>: <var>result</var=
> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#str=
ing" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A0">string</a>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <var>result</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"serialize a JavaScript value =
to JSON bytes">
    <p>To
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=
=3D"serialize a JavaScript value to JSON bytes|serialize JSON to bytes" id=
=3D"serialize-a-javascript-value-to-json-bytes">serialize a JavaScript valu=
e to JSON bytes</dfn>,
given a JavaScript value <var>value</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>string</var> be the result of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" h=
ref=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#serialize-a-javascript-value-to-a-jso=
n-string" id=3D"ref-for-serialize-a-javascript-value-to-a-json-string">seri=
alizing a JavaScript value to a JSON string</a> given
 <var>value</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return the result of running <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"htt=
ps://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-encode" id=3D"ref-for-utf-8-encode=E2=
=91=A2">UTF-8 encode</a> on <var>string</var>. <a data-link-type=3D"biblio"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-encoding" title=3D"Encoding =
Standard">[ENCODING]</a>
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <hr>
   <p>The above operations operate on JavaScript values directly; in partic=
ular, this means that
the involved objects or arrays are tied to a particular <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#realm" id=3D"ref-for-realm=
">JavaScript realm</a>. In
standards, it is often more convenient to convert between JSON and realm-in=
dependent <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A5">maps</a>,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=
=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A2">lists</a>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" hr=
ef=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=
=E2=91=A1">strings</a>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spe=
c.whatwg.org/#boolean" id=3D"ref-for-boolean=E2=91=A1">booleans</a>, number=
s, and nulls.

</p>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"parse a JSON string to an Inf=
ra value">
    <p>To
<dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D"" data-lt=
=3D"parse a JSON string to an Infra value|parse JSON into Infra values" id=
=3D"parse-a-json-string-to-an-infra-value">parse a JSON string to an Infra =
value</dfn>,
given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#st=
ring" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A2">string</a> <var>string</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>jsValue</var> be ? <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=
=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-call" id=3D"ref-for-sec-call=E2=91=
=A1">Call</a>(<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma=
262/#sec-json.parse" id=3D"ref-for-sec-json.parse=E2=91=A0">%JSON.parse%</a=
>, undefined, =C2=AB <var>string</var> =C2=BB).

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return the result of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://inf=
ra.spec.whatwg.org/#convert-a-json-derived-javascript-value-to-an-infra-val=
ue" id=3D"ref-for-convert-a-json-derived-javascript-value-to-an-infra-value=
">converting a JSON-derived JavaScript value to an Infra value</a>, given
 <var>jsValue</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"parse JSON bytes to an Infra =
value">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D""=
 id=3D"parse-json-bytes-to-an-infra-value">parse JSON bytes to an Infra val=
ue</dfn>, given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.what=
wg.org/#byte-sequence" id=3D"ref-for-byte-sequence=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">byte =
sequence</a> <var>bytes</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>string</var> be the result of running <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-decode" id=3D"ref-=
for-utf-8-decode=E2=91=A3">UTF-8 decode</a> on <var>bytes</var>. <a data-li=
nk-type=3D"biblio" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-encoding" =
title=3D"Encoding Standard">[ENCODING]</a>

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return the result of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://inf=
ra.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-a-json-string-to-an-infra-value" id=3D"ref-for-pa=
rse-a-json-string-to-an-infra-value">parsing a JSON string to an Infra valu=
e</a> given <var>string</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"convert a JSON-derived JavaSc=
ript value to an Infra value">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-noexport=3D=
"" id=3D"convert-a-json-derived-javascript-value-to-an-infra-value">convert=
 a JSON-derived JavaScript value to an Infra value</dfn>, given a JavaScrip=
t value
<var>jsValue</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>If <var>jsValue</var> is <emu-val>null</emu-val>, <var>jsValue</va=
r> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-ec=
mascript-language-types-boolean-type" id=3D"ref-for-sec-ecmascript-language=
-types-boolean-type">is a Boolean</a>, <var>jsValue</var>
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" data-refhint-key=3D"383964c1" href=3D"https://tc=
39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type" id=3D"ref-=
for-sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type=E2=91=A0">is a String</a>, or=
 <var>jsValue</var> <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.i=
o/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-number-type" id=3D"ref-for-sec-ecm=
ascript-language-types-number-type">is a Number</a>, then return <var>jsVal=
ue</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>If <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc39.github.i=
o/ecma262/#sec-isarray" id=3D"ref-for-sec-isarray">IsArray</a>(<var>jsValue=
</var>) is true:

   </p>
      <ol>
       <li>
        <p>Let <var>result</var> be an empty <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5=E2=91=
=A3">list</a>.

    </p>
       </li><li>
        <p>Let <var>length</var> be ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" hre=
f=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-tolength" id=3D"ref-for-sec-toleng=
th">ToLength</a>(! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc39.g=
ithub.io/ecma262/#sec-get-o-p" id=3D"ref-for-sec-get-o-p">Get</a>(<var>jsVa=
lue</var>, "<code>length</code>")).

    </p>
       </li><li>
        <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">For each</a> <=
var>index</var> of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.wha=
twg.org/#the-range" id=3D"ref-for-the-range=E2=91=A0">the range</a> 0 to <v=
ar>length</var> =E2=88=92 1, inclusive:

      </p>
        <ol>
         <li>
          <p>Let <var>indexName</var> be ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op=
" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-tostring" id=3D"ref-for-sec-t=
ostring">ToString</a>(<var>index</var>).

       </p>
         </li><li>
          <p>Let <var>jsValueAtIndex</var> be ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstra=
ct-op" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-get-o-p" id=3D"ref-for-s=
ec-get-o-p=E2=91=A0">Get</a>(<var>jsValue</var>, <var>indexName</var>).

       </p>
         </li><li>
          <p>Let <var>infraValueAtIndex</var> be the result of <a data-link=
-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#convert-a-json-derived=
-javascript-value-to-an-infra-value" id=3D"ref-for-convert-a-json-derived-j=
avascript-value-to-an-infra-value=E2=91=A0">converting a JSON-derived JavaS=
cript value to an Infra value</a>,
       given <var>jsValueAtIndex</var>.

       </p>
         </li><li>
          <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.or=
g/#list-append" id=3D"ref-for-list-append=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">Append</a> <va=
r>infraValueAtIndex</var> to <var>result</var>.
      </p>
        </li></ol>
       </li><li>
        <p>Return <var>result</var>.
   </p>
      </li></ol>
     </li><li>
      <p>Let <var>result</var> be an empty <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=
=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=
=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A6">ordered map</a>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#l=
ist-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">For each</a> <va=
r>key</var> of ! <var>jsValue</var>.[[OwnPropertyKeys]]():

   </p>
      <ol>
       <li>
        <p>Let <var>jsValueAtKey</var> be ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-o=
p" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-get-o-p" id=3D"ref-for-sec-g=
et-o-p=E2=91=A1">Get</a>(<var>jsValue</var>, <var>key</var>).

    </p>
       </li><li>
        <p>Let <var>infraValueAtKey</var> be the result of <a data-link-typ=
e=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#convert-a-json-derived-jav=
ascript-value-to-an-infra-value" id=3D"ref-for-convert-a-json-derived-javas=
cript-value-to-an-infra-value=E2=91=A1">converting a JSON-derived JavaScrip=
t value to an Infra value</a>,
    given <var>jsValueAtKey</var>.

    </p>
       </li><li>
        <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#map-set" id=3D"ref-for-map-set=E2=91=A2">Set</a> <var>result</var>[<var>ke=
y</var>] to <var>infraValueAtKey</var>.
   </p>
      </li></ol>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <var>result</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"serialize an Infra value to a=
 JSON string">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D""=
 id=3D"serialize-an-infra-value-to-a-json-string">serialize an Infra value =
to a JSON string</dfn>, given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://i=
nfra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A3">strin=
g</a>,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#boolean" i=
d=3D"ref-for-boolean=E2=91=A2">boolean</a>, number, null, <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A5=E2=91=A4">list</a>, or <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://inf=
ra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A4">string<=
/a>-keyed <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A7">map</a> <var>valu=
e</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>jsValue</var> be the result of
 <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#convert-a=
n-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value" id=3D"ref-for-convert-=
an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value">converting an Infra v=
alue to a JSON-compatible JavaScript value</a>, given <var>value</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc39.gi=
thub.io/ecma262/#sec-call" id=3D"ref-for-sec-call=E2=91=A2">Call</a>(<a dat=
a-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-json.string=
ify" id=3D"ref-for-sec-json.stringify=E2=91=A1">%JSON.stringify%</a>, undef=
ined, =C2=AB <var>jsValue</var> =C2=BB).

  </p>
      <p class=3D"note" role=3D"note">Since no additional arguments are pas=
sed to <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#se=
c-json.stringify" id=3D"ref-for-sec-json.stringify=E2=91=A2">%JSON.stringif=
y%</a>, the resulting
  string will have no whitespace inserted.
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"serialize an Infra value to J=
SON bytes">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D""=
 id=3D"serialize-an-infra-value-to-json-bytes">serialize an Infra value to =
JSON bytes</dfn>, given a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.s=
pec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A5">string</a>,
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#boolean" i=
d=3D"ref-for-boolean=E2=91=A3">boolean</a>, number, null, <a data-link-type=
=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=
=91=A5=E2=91=A5">list</a>, or <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://inf=
ra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A6">string<=
/a>-keyed <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#=
ordered-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A8">map</a> <var>valu=
e</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>Let <var>string</var> be the result of <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" h=
ref=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#serialize-an-infra-value-to-a-json-st=
ring" id=3D"ref-for-serialize-an-infra-value-to-a-json-string">serializing =
an Infra value to a JSON string</a>, given
 <var>value</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return the result of running <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"htt=
ps://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-encode" id=3D"ref-for-utf-8-encode=E2=
=91=A3">UTF-8 encode</a> on <var>string</var>. <a data-link-type=3D"biblio"=
 href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#biblio-encoding" title=3D"Encoding =
Standard">[ENCODING]</a>
</p>
    </li></ol>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"algorithm" data-algorithm=3D"convert an Infra value to a J=
SON-compatible JavaScript value">
    <p>To <dfn class=3D"dfn-paneled" data-dfn-type=3D"dfn" data-export=3D""=
 id=3D"convert-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value">conver=
t an Infra value to a JSON-compatible JavaScript value</dfn>, given <var>va=
lue</var>:

</p>
    <ol>
     <li>
      <p>If <var>value</var> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:/=
/infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A7">str=
ing</a>, <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#b=
oolean" id=3D"ref-for-boolean=E2=91=A4">boolean</a>, number, or null, then =
return <var>value</var>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>If <var>value</var> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https:/=
/infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=3D"ref-for-list=E2=91=A5=E2=91=A6">list</a=
>:

  </p>
      <ol>
       <li>
        <p>Let <var>jsValue</var> be ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" hr=
ef=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-arraycreate" id=3D"ref-for-sec-ar=
raycreate">ArrayCreate</a>(0).

   </p>
       </li><li>
        <p>Let <var>i</var> be 0.

   </p>
       </li><li>
        <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#list-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A1">For each</a> <=
var>listItem</var> of <var>value</var>:

    </p>
        <ol>
         <li>
          <p>Let <var>listItemJSValue</var> be the result of
     <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#conve=
rt-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value" id=3D"ref-for-conv=
ert-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value=E2=91=A0">converti=
ng an Infra value to a JSON-compatible JavaScript value</a>, given <var>lis=
tItem</var>.

     </p>
         </li><li>
          <p>Perform ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc=
39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-createdatapropertyorthrow" id=3D"ref-for-sec-crea=
tedatapropertyorthrow">CreateDataPropertyOrThrow</a>(<var>jsValue</var>, ! =
<a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#s=
ec-tostring" id=3D"ref-for-sec-tostring=E2=91=A0">ToString</a>(<var>i</var>=
),
     <var>listItemJSValue</var>).

     </p>
         </li><li>
          <p>Set <var>i</var> to <var>i</var> + 1.
    </p>
        </li></ol>
       </li><li>
        <p>Return <var>jsValue</var>.
  </p>
      </li></ol>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#a=
ssert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A1=E2=93=AA">Assert</a>: <var>value</var>=
 is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#orde=
red-map" id=3D"ref-for-ordered-map=E2=91=A2=E2=93=AA">map</a>.

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p>Let <var>jsValue</var> be ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=
=3D"https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-ordinaryobjectcreate" id=3D"ref-for=
-sec-ordinaryobjectcreate">OrdinaryObjectCreate</a>(null).

 </p>
     </li><li>
      <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#l=
ist-iterate" id=3D"ref-for-list-iterate=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A2">For each</a> <va=
r>mapKey</var> =E2=86=92 <var>mapValue</var> of <var>value</var>:

  </p>
      <ol>
       <li>
        <p><a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/=
#assert" id=3D"ref-for-assert=E2=91=A1=E2=91=A0">Assert</a>: <var>mapKey</v=
ar> is a <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#s=
tring" id=3D"ref-for-string=E2=91=A6=E2=91=A8">string</a>.

   </p>
       </li><li>
        <p>Let <var>mapValueJSValue</var> be the result of
   <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#convert=
-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value" id=3D"ref-for-conver=
t-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-value=E2=91=A1">converting=
 an Infra value to a JSON-compatible JavaScript value</a>, given <var>mapVa=
lue</var>.

   </p>
       </li><li>
        <p>Perform ! <a data-link-type=3D"abstract-op" href=3D"https://tc39=
.github.io/ecma262/#sec-createdatapropertyorthrow" id=3D"ref-for-sec-create=
datapropertyorthrow=E2=91=A0">CreateDataPropertyOrThrow</a>(<var>jsValue</v=
ar>, <var>mapKey</var>, <var>mapValueJSValue</var>).
  </p>
      </li></ol>
     </li><li>
      <p>Return <var>jsValue</var>.
</p>
    </li></ol>
    <p class=3D"warning">Because it is rarely appropriate to manipulate Jav=
aScript values directly in
specifications, prefer using <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infr=
a.spec.whatwg.org/#serialize-an-infra-value-to-a-json-string" id=3D"ref-for=
-serialize-an-infra-value-to-a-json-string=E2=91=A0">serialize an Infra val=
ue to a JSON string</a> or
<a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#serialize-=
an-infra-value-to-json-bytes" id=3D"ref-for-serialize-an-infra-value-to-jso=
n-bytes">serialize an Infra value to JSON bytes</a> instead of using this a=
lgorithm. Please
<a href=3D"https://github.com/whatwg/infra/issues/new">file an issue</a> to=
 discuss your use case if
you believe you need to use <a data-link-type=3D"dfn" href=3D"https://infra=
.spec.whatwg.org/#convert-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-va=
lue" id=3D"ref-for-convert-an-infra-value-to-a-json-compatible-javascript-v=
alue=E2=91=A2">convert an Infra value to a JSON-compatible JavaScript value=
</a>.
</p>
